TargaScript Format Specifiers and printf
=======================================

1. Basic Format Specifiers:
  Integer (%d):
    Decimal: 42

    Negative: -42

  Float (%f):
    Default precision: 3.141590

    Two decimal places: 3.14

    Zero decimal places: 3

  Boolean (%t):
    True: true

    False: false

  String (%s):
    Hello: Hello, World!

    Empty string: ''


2. Multiple Values:
  Alice is 30 years old and 5.8 feet tall.


3. Expressions in Format:
  5 + 10 = 15

  Current length of name: 5

  Age in 5 years: 35


4. Formatting Composite Types:
  Array Formatting:
    Complete array: [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]

    First element: 1

    Array length: 5

  Object Formatting:
    Complete object: {"name": "Bob", "age": 25, "city": "New York"}

    Person's name: Bob

    Person's age: 25


5. Width and Alignment:
  Right Alignment (Default):
    |   42|

    |     hello|

  Left Alignment:
    |42   |

    |hello     |

  Zero Padding (Numbers):
    |00042|

    |0003.14|


6. Precision for Floating Point:
  Default: 3.141593

  One decimal: 3.1

  Four decimals: 3.1416

  Zero decimals: 3


7. Width and Precision Combined:
  |      3.14|

  |3.14      |


8. Practical Example - Product Inventory:
  PRODUCT INVENTORY REPORT
  ========================
  ID  | Name            | Price    | Stock | Value
  ----|-----------------|----------|-------|----------
  101 | Laptop          | $ 1299.99 |    15 | $ 19499.85

  205 | Smartphone      | $  699.50 |    42 | $ 29379.00

  316 | Wireless Earbuds | $  149.00 |    78 | $ 11622.00

  ========================
  TOTAL INVENTORY VALUE: $   60500.85


Format specifiers and printf demonstration completed!
